WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:07.581
Every gate's collection supports NIST
special publication eight hundred fifty-three

3
00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:12.785
S A nine, part c, monitoring external
service providers on an ongoing basis,

4
00:00:12.785 --> 00:00:17.051
and S I five, part a, receiving
security alerts and advisories.

5
00:00:17.051 --> 00:00:21.938
The record supports S I five and
C A seven, continuous monitoring.

6
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:26.325
The evidence is the raw responses,
the notices and the manifest,

7
00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:31.977
which lists every call with its role; the
notices as one record each, valid against

8
00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:37.376
the schema; and a re-read that changes no
fingerprint, so a notice is routed once.

9
00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:39.888
The record is evidence for these controls.

10
00:00:39.888 --> 00:00:44.327
Your organization still sets their
parameters, policy and procedures,

11
00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:47.563
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

12
00:00:47.563 --> 00:00:52.200
K S I's are FedRAMP twenty X indicators
for cloud service providers.

13
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.709
The agency lines this evidence up
with what its providers report;

14
00:00:56.709 --> 00:00:58.713
it doesn't report K S I's itself.

15
00:00:58.713 --> 00:01:02.020
Which file supports which
indicator is the program's mapping.
